# Go tooling writes LF and gofmt treats a CRLF file as unformatted, so `gofmt
# -l` reports the whole file. Left to core.autocrlf (true on Windows) the .go
# files come back out of a checkout with CRLF and every one of them is flagged.
# Pinning them here keeps the working tree matching what gofmt produces.
*.go text eol=lf
